/-!
# Certificate soundness

Soundness lemmas for kernel-checked certificates: the theorems that turn a
passing finite check into a mathematical statement, together with the
packed-`Nat` arithmetic in which the checks are written.

- `Certificate.PackedDigits`: tables packed into fixed-width lanes of a
  natural number (`lane`, `packF`), and the lane-by-lane action of bitwise
  operations, arithmetic and shifts.
- `Certificate.OrbitPackedExtra`: sentinel-bit comparisons (`≤`, `=`, bounds)
  of every entry of a packed table at once.
- `Certificate.PackedLaneShifts`: masked shifts inside the lanes of a packed
  table.
- `Certificate.PackedEquality`: packed equality flags and strict comparison.
- `Certificate.PackedPopcount`: parallel popcounts by pair-summing stages, and
  the 128-bit-lane instance.
- `Certificate.PackedPopcount32`: the parallel popcount on 32-bit lanes.
- `Certificate.PackedGrid`: packed rectangular tables and broadcasting along
  rows and columns.
- `Certificate.MaskLinear`: window reconstructions of bitmasks as linear maps
  of `𝔽₂`-chains, and injectivity from a decoder checked on point masses.
- `Certificate.BatchLinear`: window reconstruction applied to every lane of a
  packed table of masks.
- `Certificate.PackedListCertificate`: packed certificates given as explicit
  lists.
- `Certificate.DualCover`: dual witnesses excluding subset-sum solutions.
- `Certificate.OrbitCensus`: complete censuses of a finite invariant set by
  canonical orbit representatives.
- `Certificate.OrbitIndexedCensus`: orbit censuses indexed by a finite type.
- `Certificate.TrimChecks`: homological codes restricted to a selection of
  checks; cycles, boundaries and the stabilizer group are unchanged when the
  dropped checks are generated by the kept ones.
-/
